# Where a Claude Code session for this repo should run.
# Read by the launch-session skill. Committed on purpose: the decision is made
# once, travels with the repo, and is reviewable in a diff.
#
# Decided 2026-09-12 when the Rules Sector was carved out of the Core by
# zkyhax-empire ADR 0005. Until then this repo had no session of its own at all --
# it was read by every other container as a read-only mount and edited from
# whichever host session happened to be open.
#
# target=container is the whole point of the ADR, not a convenience. The office
# that authors the rules every other Sector obeys must NOT be the office with the
# most privilege: a host session here would read ~/.ssh, all of ~/secrets/
# including the sleeping-dragon DR passphrase, and every repo on the box, uncapped.
# Giving the rules-writer that reach was one of the two resolutions the Emperor
# rejected. Do not change this line without re-reading ADR 0005.
#
# permission_mode is deliberately EMPTY rather than acceptEdits, which every other
# agent-container repo on this box sets. Standing order 2 of the charter: author
# the gate specification, do not build or deploy the gate -- the dispatcher, the
# settings.json files and the installer belong to the Core. The default permission
# mode is the cheapest instrument that puts a prompt in front of reaching for the
# machine.
#
# Note for other machines reading this file: zkyhax-svr's stack definition is NOT
# in this repo, on purpose -- this is the public cross-machine rules library, and a
# compose file naming one host's uid, secrets path and memory budget does not
# belong in it. It lives in zkyhax-svr-config/host/compose.rules.yaml.
target=container
container=rules-agent
workdir=/app/agentic-ai-rules-and-skills
model=opus
rc=rules-svr
tmux=rules-svr
permission_mode=
